{
 "encounter_id": "00633",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello, doctor. I'm sorry to bother you again, I just don't like the look of my wound."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "You're not bothering me, that's why we're here. Which wound is this? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The one from my hernia operation. I had it done two weeks ago, on the left side."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what's wrong with it? What are you noticing?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The skin round it has gone red, and it's warm. It was fine last week and then, um, over the weekend it changed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever or shivering with it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, no fever. I've felt a bit tired, but I've no temperature."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. I'll look in a moment, but first, let's go through your medicines, because I know there's a few."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. The antibiotic they gave me, flucloxacillin, maybe 500 mg, four times a day, I think? I'd have to check the box. Then paracetamol, 1 gram, when I need it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's maybe 500 mg of the flucloxacillin, we'll check the box, thank you. What else?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ramipril, 2.5 mg once a day. Simvastatin, 20 mg at night. And my metformin, 500 mg twice a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good, that matches what I've got. And your background conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol. All the usual suspects."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I gave up two years ago after the diagnosis. Never going back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Well done. Let me check your temperature and pulse. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Temperature 37.2, pulse 84.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Just a touch warm, but no fever. Let's see this wound. Lie back for me. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's feeling tight when I move. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The skin around the wound is red and warm for about three centimetres, with no pus, and the stitches look intact.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it infected? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's a bit of inflammation, so I'd like to take a swab from it, to see if any germs are growing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Does it hurt? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hardly at all, it's a cotton bud. Done.",
   "pause": 8.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Phew. And what about my antibiotic? Should I stay on it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, finish the course as prescribed, and I'll check the swab before changing anything. Keep the wound clean and dry."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've been covering it with a plaster. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Leave it uncovered at home if you can, and change the plaster if it gets damp. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right, I'll do that. And if it gets worse? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the redness spreads, or you get a temperature or a lot of pain, come back to me straight away or go to the urgent care centre."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take care, Mr Fisher. ~"
  }
 ],
